      {
         "id": "SECTION_prerequisites",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><span id=\"htZoomImageMsg\"></span></p><div class=\"text-store\" style=\"display:none\"><span id=\"atwWordRepresent\">Represent the number:</span><span id=\"atwWordMissing\">Which number is missing in the sequence?</span><span id=\"atwWordValue\">Value</span><span id=\"atwWordLevel\">Level</span><span id=\"atwWordNewRound\">New round</span><span id=\"atwWordNextLevel\">Next level</span><span id=\"atwWordRestart\">Restart</span><span id=\"atwWordCorrect\">&#10003; Correct!</span><span id=\"atwWordAdd\">Add one</span><span id=\"atwWordRemove\">Remove one</span></div>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "### Prerequisites\n\nIn this class we take a tour of some of the first counting tools created by humanity. Before starting, we suggest studying the earlier lessons of First Steps, especially **Our sides are equal** (<htcite0>), **Counting** (<htcite1>) and **Beyond fingers** (<htcite2>).",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "20b14681-88c0-438a-a273-a0902ae5db38",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Our sides are equal",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2023",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "3874d1e8-0f76-4432-9ee2-d8c8c9dccf53",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Counting",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "cc8c1467-a6af-4f9c-ba60-ab6df35aba05",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Beyond fingers",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_introduction",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Introduction\n\nHumanity spread across the world over almost 2 million years. If we consider only our own species, *Homo sapiens*, this expansion is much shorter: less than 300,000 years (<htcite0>).\n\nAlong that journey, different peoples created their own ways of counting. In this class we take a tour of some of these first tools and of the regions where they appeared.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a4f22e25-5839-407f-a1aa-634521d52b42",
                     "text": "González Redondo, Francisco A., et al.",
                     "page": "pp. 174 - 177, 180 - 182",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2010",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-brain\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection 1: One origin or many?</b><br /><br />Do you think mathematical knowledge arose in a single place and then spread, or did it appear independently in different regions?</div></div></center></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_mathematics",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### The Evolution of Mathematics\n\nMathematical knowledge developed independently in different places and was only later unified by our species (<htcite0>). In this class we highlight maps and the approximate periods when each numerical system appeared, according to our current understanding.\n\nThe map below shows the journey of our species across the world (<htcite1>).",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a4f22e25-5839-407f-a1aa-634521d52b42",
                     "text": "González Redondo, Francisco A., et al.",
                     "page": "pp. 174 - 177, 180 - 182",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2010",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "10cd855b-c2dc-4045-8a6c-f8486ef67cfa",
                     "text": "Mapswire",
                     "page": "https://mapswire.com",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"atwImgJourney\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('atwImgJourney', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 1</b>: The journey of <i>Homo sapiens</i> across the world. Map from Mapswire (<htcite0>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "10cd855b-c2dc-4045-8a6c-f8486ef67cfa",
                     "text": "Mapswire",
                     "page": "https://mapswire.com",
