            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_africa",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### In Africa: Counting with Bones\n\nThe first counting system we know of arose in Africa, about 37,000 years ago. It was inspired by our hands and was recorded with marks made on bones (<htcite0>). Scholars such as Francisco A. González Redondo study these marks to understand when counting began.\n\nThe game below uses the same idea: observe the number and place the same quantity of marks on the bone.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a4f22e25-5839-407f-a1aa-634521d52b42",
                     "text": "González Redondo, Francisco A., et al.",
                     "page": "pp. 174 - 177, 180 - 182",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2010",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"atwImgAfrica\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('atwImgAfrica', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 2</b>: Africa on the world map. Map from Mapswire (<htcite0>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "10cd855b-c2dc-4045-8a6c-f8486ef67cfa",
                     "text": "Mapswire",
                     "page": "https://mapswire.com",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<div class=\"atw-game\" data-atw=\"bones\"></div>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_quipu",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### In America: The Quipus\n\nThe second counting system we study did not arise near the first one. The earliest evidence dates from about 5,000 years ago, in Caral, Peru, although researchers still debate how old the quipus are (<htcite0>).\n\nThe quipu is read on the vertical cords that hang from the main cord, and each knot represents a count. Add knots until the cord shows the proposed number.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "4f8542c9-f060-4d3c-8a67-971b6d63e1ff",
                     "text": "Ascher, M., & Ascher, R.",
                     "page": "Mathematics of the Incas: Code of the Quipu",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2013",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"atwImgSouthAmerica\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('atwImgSouthAmerica', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 3</b>: South America on the world map. Map from Mapswire (<htcite0>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "10cd855b-c2dc-4045-8a6c-f8486ef67cfa",
                     "text": "Mapswire",
                     "page": "https://mapswire.com",
                     "date_time": {
