      {
         "id": "SECTION_china",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### In Asia (China): The Suanpan\n\nAround <htdate0> we have the first information about the *suanpan* (算盤), the Chinese abacus. This abacus differs from the *calculi* because it has a different number of beads (<htcite0>).\n\nWrite the proposed number on the suanpan by moving the beads.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "c3c69877-a92b-493c-b98a-5c1c6d5875f4",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Building to count (Suanpan, 算盤)",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "-190",
                     "month": "",
                     "day": ""
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"atwImgAsia2\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('atwImgAsia2', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 7</b>: Asia on the world map. Map from Mapswire (<htcite0>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "10cd855b-c2dc-4045-8a6c-f8486ef67cfa",
                     "text": "Mapswire",
                     "page": "https://mapswire.com",
