            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_yupana",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### In America: The Yupana\n\nReturning to America (*Abya Yala*), we know that the Incas — during the 15th and 16th centuries according to the Gregorian calendar — created a tool to do mathematics. There is also evidence that the *yupana* was used together with the *quipus* (<htcite0>; <htcite1>).\n\nOn the yupana, each row holds one digit and the seeds are placed over the grid. Use the buttons to represent the proposed number.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "5dbd2e9f-5631-407e-9b80-e3a5d4f8838f",
                     "text": "Prem, Dhavit",
                     "page": "Matemática Inka y la Yupana",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "1bb0274d-dc51-4740-ac62-4d157b06ad88",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Yupana (Addition)",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"atwImgYupana\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('atwImgYupana', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 8</b>: South America (Tawantinsuyu) on the map. Map from Mapswire (<htcite0>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "10cd855b-c2dc-4045-8a6c-f8486ef67cfa",
                     "text": "Mapswire",
